KZ3 patch 2040 (RSX pass 40): attribute-major vertex fetch (RSX_VTX_BATCH).
rsx_vertex_compact.c/.h: rsx_vertex_fetch_many(plan, refs, count, out, out_stride) converts a draw's unique
vertices in blocks of 128, one layout slot at a time, with the element type and component count resolved once
per block and slot (specialised loops per type x components); a vertex outside the attribute's contiguous
mapping, a frequency-divided attribute, CMP32 and unmapped attributes take the per-vertex path, which is the
slot body of rsx_vertex_fetch_one (now shared as rsx_vertex_fetch_attr_one). The per-component arithmetic is
the same expression as rsx_vertex_decode_fast, so the payload bytes are identical; host test
tools/smoke/test_vtx_batch.sh compares both paths byte for byte (every type, defaults, dividers, fallbacks,
inline streams, counts around the block size) and times them.
rsx_live_draw.c: the compact-payload fetch loop calls it when RSX_VTX_BATCH is on (default in
LD_VTX_BATCH_DEFAULT = 1 since pass 41; RSX_VTX_BATCH=0 keeps the per-vertex loop). Log: [vtx-batch] once at the first draw.
Upstream candidate (pure refactor of the fetch loop, no KZ3-specific behaviour).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): shrunk: upstream has the attribute-major rsx_vertex_fetch_many (no out_stride arg, writes at layout.stride); 2040 keeps only LD_VTX_BATCH's call in live_draw; tools/smoke/test_vtx_batch.c calls upstream's signature.

